# Backend stability — client-first changes

Fleetbase backend (`packages/*`, Laravel routes/controllers, Docker services) is well structured. **Do not change it by default.**

## Default approach

1. Fix in **frontend** (`frontend/`), **mobile** (`fleet_mobile-main/`), **E2E helpers**, or **config/env** first.
2. Align clients to existing **`/int/v1`** contracts — do not invent new endpoints for convenience.
3. Handle idempotent API responses on the client (e.g. "already dispatched") instead of retrying every legacy URL/method.

## When backend changes are allowed

Only if **all** are true:

- The bug is clearly server-side (wrong validation, missing route that clients legitimately need, data corruption).
- No workable client-side fix exists (mapper, query param, guard, single canonical API call).
- The diff is **minimal** and scoped to the failure — no drive-by refactors.

## Do not disturb

- Onboarding/installer safeguards (`InstallerSchemaReset`, `InstallerMigrationPaths`, extension migration registration).
- Existing API contracts used by console, mobile, and Playwright unless explicitly requested.

## Examples

```javascript
// ❌ BAD — retry storm across wrong endpoints
for (const method of ["patch", "post"]) {
  await api.patch(`/orders/${id}/dispatch`);
  await api.patch("/orders/dispatch", { orders: [id] });
}

// ✅ GOOD — one canonical internal call + idempotent handling
await api.patch("/orders/dispatch", { order: id });
// treat "already dispatched" as success when appropriate
```

```text
❌ BAD — add internal route because mobile guessed wrong path once
✅ GOOD — fix mobile service to call existing `/drivers/{id}/track`
```
